  "narrative": "3.84(d) \n   \nCleaning, sanitization, housekeeping, and pest control. \nIn the primary enclosure housing 2 Bonnet macaques, 1 pigtail macaque, and 1 crab-eating macaque, numerous rats \nwere observed on the ground and running along the metal beams and mesh wiring of the enclosure about six feet up on \nthe east wall of the enclosure. \nThe presence of rats is a potential disease hazard to the animals. Rodents can carry diseases and parasites which can \nspread to the primates in the enclosure. \nAn effective program for control of insects, external parasites, and birds and mammals that are pests, must be established \nand maintained so as to promote the health and well-being of the animals and reduce contamination by pests in animal \nareas. \n \nTo be corrected by August 31, 2026. \n \nThis inspection and exit interview were conducted with facility representatives. \n \nAdditional Inspectors: \nRonald Richardson, VETERINARY MEDICAL OFFICER n",
